{
  "note": [
    "The Comm Room's fabric (DR-113), cut from the one tower layout in scripts/fabric-tower.mjs -- regenerate from there, do not hand-edit. COMM-ROOM.metadata.json v2: a regular octagon, apothem 3.2 (6.4 across the flats, 6.93 across the corners), 3 m high, its walls centred on bearings 0, 45, 90 and so on -- the tower's own axis, the one the core's two passages are cut on. The receive console fills the north-west wall, the send console the south-east, the doorway is the south-west wall and the cable trunk climbs the north-east; the four views land on those and the four seams on the plain walls between them.",
    "The game: \"a small room with no windows. The sole exit is southwest. Two wide consoles fill either end of the room; thick cables lead up into the ceiling\" (compone.zil 2822-2828). The red \"Tranzmishun Reeseevd\" lamp is the room's referable light, not a ceiling fitting (rules/connectors.js 271-275); the enunciator's panel is drawn once with every lamp dark and the flashing one is an engine OVERLAY on its own CHEMICAL-REQUIRED value, dark once COMM-FIXED or COMM-SHUTDOWN. The seven lamps are NOT fabric: COMM-ROOM.metadata.json's `overlays` hangs each as a `cutout` cut square-on out of TURN-135's own painted lens and re-lit in its canon colour (compone.zil 2854-2869), which is how all seven carry colours the palette has not got.",
    "Out through the doorway, along the 45-degree line the room shares with the core and the deck: 0.80 m of passage, then the core's drum -- its curved wall, its worn floor, the stair standing due west of its centre and the cool lamp over it -- and straight on through the core's south-west gap, the Observation Deck's daylight and the sea over its parapet. The elevator door is NOT in sight: it lies at bearing 250 from this eye and the passage holds every ray inside 215 to 235."
  ],
